The SCXML 1.0 Implementation Report Plan test suite in this directory is
copyright the World Wide Web Consortium. Its index page,
https://www.w3.org/Voice/2013/scxml-irp/, section "License", says:

    This test suite is licensed under both the W3C Test Suite License
    <https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2008/04-testsuite-license> and the
    W3C 3-clause BSD License
    <https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2008/03-bsd-license>. See W3C
    Legal's explanation of the licenses
    <https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2008/04-testsuite-copyright>.

The page's copyright notice: Copyright (c) 2015 W3C (MIT, ERCIM, Keio,
Beihang), All Rights Reserved. The stylesheets confEcma.xsl and
confXPath.xsl carry: Copyright 1998-2003 W3C (MIT, ERCIM, Keio), All
Rights Reserved. See http://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/.

W3C's explanation says the choice between the two licenses "is up to the
licensee for every single use of tests from a W3C Test Suite": the 3-clause
BSD license "for software development, bug tracking, and other
applications that do not require assertions of performance to the public
or implied claims of conformance to a W3C Specification", and the W3C test
suite license, which permits no modification, "when claims of performance
with respect to a specification are required".

tinyactors uses the files under the 3-clause BSD license: it runs them to
develop and test its software. The files here are unmodified; the
translations made from them (build/w3c, build/scenarios) are not kept in
git. A claim of conformance to SCXML 1.0 would have to be made against the
unaltered tests under the W3C test suite license.

